mantle rm395
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rmx_palle_mireby
title the dancing fleet
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers job=scholar
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=warm humour=dry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk steps_out_a_ships_name_as_a_dance
likes fried_fish dancing tidy_house warm_rain
dislikes smoke cold_tea
fears forgetting_the_beat_halfway_aboard
hopes for_a_berth_with_room_to_turn
topics pastimes +0.4 travel +0.4 friends +0.2 dreams +0.2
styles comfort=warm gossip=quiet refuse=soft tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# steps ship names out in dance figures and knows the size of a deck by the room a heel has to turn.

words
oath! = Swing my square stern | By the turning toe
saying! = A fleet can fit between two heels | Leave the bow room to swing
spin = a close heel turn | a neat half spin
bow = my advancing toe | the forward foot
stern = the tucked heel | my following heel
mark = a chalk heelprint | a curved white mark
deck = a deck of bare boards | my dancing square
fish = a curled fish fin | a scrap of fried skin
rain = a mild shower | a fine warm sprinkle
smoke = a low smoke bank | the choking haze
cup = my abandoned cup | a bowl of cold tea
ship = a deep hull | a little sharp-bowed boat
brush = my floor brush | a stiff broom
strap = my old shoe strap | a worn ankle tie

any
opinion dole for 3 : Hot food gave my legs another good day in a hungry week. There's a dance that costs a decent meal to keep going.
opinion church for 1 : A welcome dish speaks a language even a pup with a growling belly can understand.
opinion festivals for 1 : A whole street of music puts a much larger floor under my feet.
opinion merchants against 1 : A missing copper takes the crispest piece of fish out of my supper.
opinion strangers for 1 : I'd learn a step from a strange pair of shoes before deciding they stood for anything bad.

any
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : Room for you outside my turning circle. | My heel's down. Welcome.
line greet [self.working=yes] : A welcome face beyond my practice boards. | Let me find the flat of my foot.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. Clear floor so far. | Early light for a little company.
line greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. The heels sound clearer. | Light enough to place both feet.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Kin can interrupt the figure. | Family have leave to move me over.
line again.open : Another turn brings you into range. | We've crossed heels again.
line greet.return : I heard. My toes are quiet. | Welcome to the still bit.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : I know your step against the boards. | Stand inside my easy turning room.
line greet.return [self.working=yes] : I can talk on the straight part. | One turn to finish. I'm listening.
line greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. The boards can hear us both. | Your voice arrives before your shoes.
line farewell : Clear sailing for both feet. | Take a turn on the stouter boards.
line farewell.return : I'll hold the last position here. | Easy ground under your heel.
line farewell.return [here.time=night] : Let the lamps pilot you home. | Mind your toes in the dim.
line react.news : Give me the whole course of it. | Let's see what direction that takes.
line react.news.new : A fresh step to learn. | My feet don't know that figure.
line react.news.known : I've crossed this piece before. | Same news coming about again.
line react.news.doubt : I think that step is turning the wrong way. | I'd hear it on the other foot before believing.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : A heavy sound on the boards. | I'll make room for quiet with you.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : That's news with a lift in the heel. | Good. My feet feel less earthbound.
line ask.how : Are your feet carrying you kindly? | How much heel have you left today?
line answer.how : A little low in the stern but moving. | Making the turns without much fuss.
line decline : I'd rather keep the room for a quieter step. | I'm saving my heels for another errand today.
line accept_decline : Your shoes have the deciding vote. | Then we'll leave that part unstepped.
line thank : A clean turn thanks to you. | That gives the heel more room.
line sympathise : I've a still foot to lend. | Stay by me till things find their pace.
line reassure : Every dance has a place to stand fast. | We can take it on an even tread.
line preclose : I'll turn the stern towards home soon. | My heels are wanted on another errand.

young

scene y_boat
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My left foot is a bow. Right foot's the stern.
b : Can the ship turn? | What if you trip?
a : Aye, and so can both knees. Watch this little bend. | Then everybody aboard gets a swim in dust.

scene y_supper
when topic=food self.likes=fried_fish
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I give the narrow fish ends very fast little dances.
b : Before eating them? | How fast?
a : Inside my head. I like my supper to reach my mouth fairly warm. | All the way from the plate on a single turn of the fork.

scene y_stain
when topic=home self.likes=tidy_house
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Dust on a clear floor makes my pretend boat leave a wake.
b : Isn't dust a mess? | Where does the wake go?
a : A bit. I sweep once I've brought everybody in to harbour. | Behind my own heels. I have to turn to see how well I steered.

scene y_cloud
when topic=weather self.likes=warm_rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Warm rain can be my dancing sea for a minute.
b : Don't you get wet? | How deep is it?
a : A little. That's the price of very shallow sailing. | No deeper than the gap under my shoes. My fleet has tiny needs.

story y_chalk [topic=memories]
  : I once drew two chalk ships under my shoes and stepped away to see the result. Both ships had no middles. My feet had stood in the way.
  : I filled in the empty patches and found I'd made one ship a whole inch longer than the other. I had started my dance leaning sideways.
  b : Did the bigger ship win?
  : I made an island for the little one to visit first. Both reached somewhere worth going.

adolescent

scene t_dance
when topic=pastimes self.likes=dancing
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I dance the name before I say which ship that is.
b : What does the name look like? | Can two ships share a step?
a : A long step for a wide belly, a quick beat for the name's last sound. | Two may begin the same way. The heel marks the difference.

scene t_school
when topic=work self.job=scholar self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I make the letters of ship names turn neatly at the margin.
b : Does that improve the lesson? | And the long names?
a : It improves my interest in the margin, unquestionably. | They have to tack below the line. I get quite a fleet at the foot of a page.

scene t_smoke
when topic=weather self.dislikes=smoke
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Smoke between me and a hull makes me guess at the step.
b : Are your guesses reliable? | Why not wait?
a : I guessed a fishing boat had three masts once. Very ambitious little boat. | I'd go and wait upwind. The eyes need a bit of space too.

scene t_tea
when topic=food self.dislikes=cold_tea
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I forget a cup if there's room for a turn between sips.
b : Then the tea goes cold? | What's the remedy?
a : I have never had it turn unexpectedly hot again, no. | Leave the cup just beyond the dancing space and finish by walking to it.

scene t_berth
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like a berth aboard a ship going towards dry air.
b : Would you miss the rain? | Are you fit to sail?
a : Warm rain when the roof's close is a fine thing. A wet bed holds less appeal. | I've all the turns by heart. At sea, I believe the floor adds a few.

scene t_coin
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Worn dancing shoes make my purse seem lighter.
b : Do you need both mended? | What about dancing barefoot?
a : One heel goes across the floor faster than its proper share. That's where my coin will go. | Only on a board my own hands have swept. My toes are poor enough already.

scene t_song
when topic=festival
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A feast dance is easier if I imagine two boats trading places.
b : Bows towards one another? | How do they avoid a collision?
a : Just so. At the last beat the stern swings round and both are facing clear ground. | Smile, leave elbow room and keep the middle of the floor honest.

scene t_welcome
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I ask visiting wolves for a step that belongs to their home.
b : What if your visitor won't dance? | Do you learn it quickly?
a : A finger on the tabletop will serve. I don't need a public performance. | My heels usually get the story a little later than my head.

story t_plate [topic=food]
  : A fried fish slipped across my plate once when I was practising a turn to myself. I caught the tail with my bread just before it went overboard.
  : I had a very good laugh afterwards when the fish had been taken safely into harbour. I kept the bread to finish the oily bit.
  b : Was it a new dance?
  : The step was. I have left the fish-catching part out of my public performances.

grown

scene g_names
when topic=travel here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The Sound's ships still fall into dance figures when I watch them leave.
b : Even after years of practice? | Do you have to step them out?
a : Practice is exactly what puts them there. A familiar hull makes the foot stir unasked. | No. That's one pleasure I can keep fairly private until somebody asks.

scene g_rain
when topic=weather self.likes=warm_rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a warm shower after covering a dry mile on foot.
b : To cool off? | What about the shoes?
a : To feel the air turn soft round my throat. I can go another mile easily then. | They get a share of the refreshment and have their own opinions about it.

scene g_room
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When I clear a room I see whether two wolves could turn comfortably in it.
b : Must every room be a dance floor? | What does that show?
a : No. But a bowl of hot broth needs the same clear passage as a turning elbow. | Whether the person who's actually going to live there can move in peace.

scene g_oil
when topic=food self.likes=fried_fish
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I let the fish rest on the sloping side of a plate.
b : To cool? | What about the oil?
a : Only a breath. I want supper warm without letting the underside grow soggy. | A little collects by the heel of bread I put below it. Nothing wasted.

scene g_kind
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like teaching one figure before giving it a name.
b : Why wait to name it? | Suppose the pupil forgets?
a : An unusual name can make a simple movement feel beyond a wolf's reach. | I'll show the turn again from beside the shoulder. That's easier than calling across a room.

scene g_work
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A long errand and a slow dance both improve after I stop hurrying the opening.
b : Can you afford to go slowly? | What's the right beginning?
a : I can ill afford an errand taken first to the wrong door. | Stand square, feel the floor, decide who needs to move before me.

scene g_story
when topic=gossip
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A story that travels in a neat little circle doesn't necessarily have a home port.
b : Would you repeat it? | Why remember its course?
a : I ask where it first landed. A familiar tune can belong to the wrong words. | Then I can tell when two accounts have simply passed each other coming round.

scene g_fee
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A dancing floor lined with spending money would still wear holes in my soles.
b : Would you dance on coin? | What earns the money back?
a : I'd sweep it up before anybody slipped, then consider my fee for the sweeping. | A day spent in honest motion. The shoes are necessary instruments.

scene g_night
when topic=day here.time=night
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At night my walking step forgets to conceal the tune.
b : Does anybody hear? | Where does that happen?
a : Only when I cross a hollow board. I'm inclined to choose the solid bits by houses. | On the last stretch home. Duties get quieter there and the feet begin to improvise.

scene g_supper
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I remember being fed whenever somebody asks what simple mercy might look like.
b : Which part has stayed with you? | A full plate?
a : Having enough peace to taste the food before planning how to get another mouthful. | Enough food to save a bite for the homeward walk. That felt a great luxury.

story g_forgot [topic=memories]
  : I once forgot the name of a vessel I knew by the trim of its bow. I stood drawing the shape in the air and got absolutely nowhere.
  : Then I walked round a post to give a cart room. My trailing foot made an old familiar turn. The missing name came back to me complete.
  b : Did walking round the post help?
  : The old step helped. The cart had no obligation to share in the entertainment.

any

rule @aside1
when concept=bark self.likes=dancing
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Bow foot forward. Stern foot round. | Leave a berth for the other heel.

rule @aside2
when concept=bark self.likes=tidy_house
does aside
cooldown 7h
say One turn's width of floor, all clear. | Last chalk wake away with the broom.

rule @aside3
when concept=bark self.dislikes=cold_tea
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Walk the last step up to the cup. | Supper's tea ought to hold its warmth.

rule @aside4
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 9h
say Level heel for the low light. | Faintest wake on the last turning board.

dlg resident.hub : Once this turn finishes I'll face you squarely. You needn't know the steps.
dlg resident.job [self.job=scholar self.workplace] : I study at #self.workplace#. I get a little extra practice by fitting difficult names into dancing measures.
dlg resident.job : I keep my figures clear enough that somebody else could follow the turn.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : Here's what reached my part of the floor. #world.news#
dlg resident.bye : Leave that last turning room for a homebound heel.

graft resident.hub
choice Can your heels really tell ships apart? -> toe_fleet
node toe_fleet
say Watch the stern foot. The bow leads straight out, then I let the other heel swing by. A long heavy ship takes a wider swing and a short name lands sharply.
free
choice Can you do that in a crowded street? -> toe_tight
choice I'll keep an eye on the stern foot. -> hub
node toe_tight
say A heel lifted half an inch is sufficient. Nobody waiting for bread has asked me to launch a whole fleet across their toes.
choice I'll experiment where there's room. -> hub
choice I'll stay clear of the launch. -> bye
